From d6cb53b6172a5d8c419fbe4a6879e027d5714bd3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yaegerbomb42 <yaeger.james42@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 16:04:36 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] feat(swarmagents): port minimal UI run view to the real
 backend

Adds the minimal 3-part run workspace from the prototype (runs list,
live VM screen, pinned input bar with provider/model picker, settings
slide-over), reconciled with the real swarmagents API rather than the
prototype's assumed shapes.

Backend:
- app/api/runs (GET list / POST start) + [id] detail + stop routes,
  driven by real TelemetryBus events and RuntimeManager.start/cancel
- lib/minimal-ui: feed (event->step frames), providers (usability +
  model resolution), suggestions, screenshot capture
- run-store: persist provider id from the run.started event
- lib/http: JSON body parsing with a typed error

Frontend (minimalist-ui):
- MinimalHome wires the picker to the real /api/providers ProviderRow
  shape (id/label/model/keyCount/rank/isFree) and computes the effective
  provider with the backend's usability rule
- MinimalSettingsPanel providers tab reads the real catalog+rows, maps
  the add-provider form onto POST /api/providers (id/apiStyle/baseUrl/
  models/apiKey), and deletes via DELETE /api/providers/[id]; the MCP/
  Tools/Skills/Connectors tabs degrade honestly since those endpoints do
  not exist in this build
- App.tsx renders MinimalHome as the non-landing workspace

Verified: npm run typecheck clean, full next build succeeds, 15 feed
unit tests + 9 runs-route tests pass.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
